── add a folder ──
 Another folder to look for git checkouts in. radar matches each checkout to
 its repo by its origin remote.

 ACCEPTS
 a full path, or one starting with ~/ (pasted links to files work too)

 NOW
 1 folder

 config: [git] roots















── detail ──
 Another folder to look for git checkouts in. radar matches each checkout to
 its repo by its origin remote.

 ACCEPTS
 a full path, or one starting with ~/ (pasted links to files work too)

 NOW
 1 folder

 config: [git] roots

 ▪ WHAT IT READS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The git checkouts under these folders, as far down as look down.
   New clones inside them show up at the next look.
   With git on this machine: branches, changes, ahead, behind.
 ⎇ WHERE IT SHOWS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Branches (B): every branch in these checkouts.
   A repo or merge request: where it is checked out, e and t.
   Agents start in the checkout you pick.
 ⚙ CHANGE IT LATER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Settings / git / checkouts
 ℹ SKIP IT? ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Branches stay empty until a folder is set.
   The services work without it.
"
`;

