"── settings ──
  ? Found: a Jira site (gamma.atlassian.net, JIRA_EMAIL). Use it?
  ? Found in your environment: a Jira site (JIRA_OTHER_URL, …). Use it?
  + add a site   paste its link, e.g. https://acme.atlassian.net
 ▌ acme   acme.atlassian.net · 2 projects
    ├─ site            https://acme.atlassian.net
    ├─ account         alice@example.com
    ├─ token           env:RADAR_JIRA_TEST_TOKEN
    ├─ signed in as    Alice Example
    ├─ check           not checked yet
    └─ projects        ABC, DEF
 ▌ beta   beta.atlassian.net · 1 project
    ├─ site            https://beta.atlassian.net
    ├─ account         alice@example.com
    ├─ token           env:RADAR_JIRA_TEST_TOKEN
    ├─ signed in as    —
    ├─ check           not checked yet
    └─ projects        XYZ
  refresh         every 2m
  on start        ask first

── found in /work/acme/.mcp.json ──
 radar found a Jira site in /work/acme/.mcp.json. Do you want to use it?

 FOUND
 gamma.atlassian.net  the site's address, as written
 JIRA_EMAIL           the account

 radar stores only the variables' names (env:NAME) and reads their values each
 time it starts. It never shows the values or saves them.

 It is the file's "tools" entry. It also watches GAM (acceptance criteria in
 customfield_10044). Its token is typed into the file: radar does not copy it,
 and asks which variable holds it.

 IF YOU USE IT
 radar adds the site gamma and asks which variable holds its token.

 ⏎ uses it








