exports[`recorded view fixtures > slack_settings-look at 80x24 1`] = `
"── settings ──
 MESSAGES
   density  how a thread's messages are laid out                        compact
   author   who wrote a message                                  links and keys
   you      the reader, in place of their own name                       accent
   pinged   a mention of you or your groups                      warning · bold
   mention  a mention of someone else, a group or a channel        third accent
   link     a link                                             info · underline
   emoji    a custom emoji, shown as its :name:                      muted text
   code     code, inline or in a block                              data string
   quote    a quoted line                               secondary text · italic
   new      what is new since you caught up                      success · bold
   time     when                                                     muted text
   channel  a channel's name                                   main text · bold
 MESSAGES TREE
   band     the shade behind every other thread                        overlays
   heading  the shade behind a day's or a group's heading              overlays
   lines    the tree lines joining threads and replies               muted text
 ALERTS
   firing   an alert that is firing                                error · bold
   failed   a job that failed                                      error · bold
   resolved an alert that resolved                                      success
   priority an alert's priority                                         warning
   unmapped an alert no rule places, and its group          muted text · italic

── density ──
 How the messages of a thread, the detail pane and a direct message are laid
 out.

 compact  in use
 One line a message: the time, the author in a column, then the text. The
 author is left blank for the same person within five minutes. A thin line
 marks a new day, and a thread's replies sit under one divider. In a narrow
 panel the author and time take a line and the text sits under it.

 cozy
 The roomier layout: the author, place and date on a line, the text under it,
 the reactions on a line of their own, a blank line between messages, and
 replies two cells in.

 config: [slack] density = "compact" or "cozy"









"
`;

